WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.150
Cars 3 brings back Lightning McQueen for the
third instalment in Pixar's Cars trilogy and,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.280
like all Pixar films, it's loaded with Pixar
and Disney easter eggs like the Pizza Planet

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.910
Truck and Cinderella's carriage.
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.740
and in this video I'll be revealing where
all the usual Pixar easter eggs including

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.370
A-1-1-3 are hidden as well as uncovering some
more obscure ones, and how the movie fits

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.740
in with the Pixar Theory.
I'm also kicking off my very special Cars

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.520
3 giveaway.
Two lucky winners will get this awesome The

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.070
Art of Cars 3 hardback book which shows off
some of Pixar's amazing concept art, storyboards

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.829
and exclusive insights into the making of
the movie.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:42.040
For a chance to win, just subscribe and leave
a comment about the film, and also answer

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.730
the question I'll be asking later in the video.
Quick warning there are spoilers ahead for

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.149
Cars 3, so take care if you haven't seen the
movie yet.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:54.879
Let's start with the Pizza Planet Truck, which
debuted in Pixar's first feature Toy Story

00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:58.040
and which has appeared in almost every Pixar
film to date.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.100
In the Cars universe, the Pizza Planet Truck
is actually a character called Todd and in

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.560
the first movie he appeared as an onlooker
at the Los Angeles International Speedway.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.500
He cameo'd twice in Cars 2, the first time
appearing on TV and, the second, as a spectator

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.130
at the Radiator Springs Grand Prix.
And in Cars 3, Pizza Planet Truck Todd is

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:21.700
a participant in the Crazy 8 demolition derby.
And in this movie, the Pizza Planet Truck's

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.700
rocket actually flies into the crowd at one
point!

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.729
Miss Fritter is a cool new character we meet
in Cars 3 who collects the license plates

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:32.969
of each of the opponents she defeats at the
Thunder Hollow Speedway.

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:37.530
Miss Fritter also carries a street sign that
appears to read "West Cutting Boulevard",

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.509
an easter egg to the location of Pixar's former
headquarters in Richmond, California.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:47.320
And this street sign last appeared in Toy
Story 3 above the door in Andy's bedroom.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.219
Also, on the side of Miss Fritter is the number
58 which the animators included as a reference

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:55.630
to the year Miss Fritter voice actress Lea
DeLaria was born.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:58.900
And the name of DeLaria's high school is also
on the bus!

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.740
By the way, I wonder if Miss Fritter's name
is a play on "Ms. Frizzle" who drives the

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.770
Magic School Bus in the animated TV series
of the same name?

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.230
The Pixar Luxo ball is also in the demolition
derby scene painted on one of the vehicles

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.340
participating in the race at Thunder Hollow
Speedway.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.370
The Luxo ball, of course, goes back to Pixar's
very first short, Luxo Jr, which features

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:24.050
both the Luxo ball and two desk lamps, one
of which appears in Pixar's logo.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:28.330
There's also a couple of A-1-1-3 easter eggs
in Cars 3.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.099
You can see one on the press sticker that
Shannon Spokes wears on her side.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:36.230
Spokes is the on-the-track reporter who's
voiced by real-life sports reporter Shannon

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:39.760
Spake.
And A-1-1-3 is also the number of Sterling's

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.120
office at the Rust-eze Racing Centre.
The A-1-1-3 easter egg has appeared in every

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.470
single Pixar movie to date and is an homage
to the classroom at California Institute of

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.190
the Arts where the likes of Pixar's John Lasseter
studied.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.771
And this one's quite hard to spot, but inside
Sterling's office, hidden among the trophies,

00:02:56.771 --> 00:02:59.870
is Cinderella's pumpkin carriage.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:03.450
And could this be an easter egg to the tree
from A Bug's Life which has also appeared

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.790
previously in Up and Toy Story 2?

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.939
Back at Thunder Hollow Speedway, there's a
sneaky easter egg to Cars 3 production designer

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:15.680
Bill Cone on the Wild Bill's Racing Cones
billboard which you can spot in the background

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.580
here.
And I wonder whether Wild Bill also provided

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.870
the cones for Sally's Cozy Cone Motel in Radiator
Springs?

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:27.060
An important easter egg in Cars 3 that links
the movie to Jon Negroni's Pixar theory is

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:32.220
the first appearance of Buy n Large, aka BnL,
in a Cars feature film, where it appears as

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.069
a track sponsor at a speedway.
BnL is the corporation in WALL•E that basically

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:41.200
enabled the pollution of the planet and sent
humans away from Earth while it attempted

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.379
to clear it up.
The Pixar Theory suggests that Cars takes

00:03:44.379 --> 00:03:48.970
place after humans leave the planet and before
a time hundreds of years later when the events

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.280
of WALL•E take place and the presence of
Buy n Large as a racetrack sponsor in Cars

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.239
3 supports this suggested timeline.

00:03:55.239 --> 00:04:01.469
Racer number 31, Terry Kargas, is sponsored
by Triple Dent Gum, the chewing gum from Inside

00:04:01.469 --> 00:04:05.739
Out with the recurring jingle that plays throughout
that movie.

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:10.819
Pixar's lucky charm John Ratzenberger returns
in Cars 3 as the voice of the truck Mack,

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.090
and there's a scene with Mack in the movie
which includes a very sneaky and obscure NASCAR

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.120
easter egg.
Before going to the demolition derby at Thunder

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.579
Hollow Speedway, Mack and Lightning decide
they want to go incognito.

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:26.870
For his disguise, Mack chooses to go as a
Jocko Flocko Party supplies truck, which is

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.419
an awesome reference to the real-life monkey
called Jocko Flocko that raced with NASCAR

00:04:31.419 --> 00:04:35.300
champ Tim Flock.
Jocko Flocko and Tim Flock drove together

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:41.150
in eight races in 1953, including Flock's
Grand National win at Hickory Motor Speedway.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.090
By the way, I wonder whether the clown on
Mack's truck disguise is also a reference

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.430
to Jangles, the clown that Riley fears in
Inside Out.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.550
Cars 3 also pays homage to NASCAR's roots
in Prohibition-era bootlegging with a moonshine

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:57.750
still that appears in the background of a
scene in the woods!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.110
And those origins also get a nod in the character
of Junior "Midnight" Moon who is voiced by

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:07.470
NASCAR legend Robert Glenn "Junior" Johnson,
who got his start in racing by making moonshine

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:12.020
runs through the mountains of North Carolina,
and more recently teamed up with a distillery

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.050
to share his family moonshine recipe which
is sold as Midnight Moon.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.930
I also liked this shot in the woods of Lightning
in silhouette leaping across the full moon

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.060
which not only has a kind of E.T. vibe to
it, but also made me think back to the first

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:30.760
Cars movie where we saw Mater in silhouette
leaping across the face of a full moon.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.090
And talking of classic movies, I think there's
shades of Rocky's story in the scenes of Lightning

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:39.850
training on the beach, the way he's competing
against a new younger rival and has to go

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:43.910
back to the drawing board to figure out what
he needs to do to win, and also how he has

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.880
to get himself a new trainer.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:51.430
As always, Pixar have included an easter egg
to their upcoming movie in the current film.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:55.670
After Cars 3, Pixar is releasing Coco, a Mexican
Day of the Dead story.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:59.729
There's already a Cars easter egg in Coco
where a young boy is wearing a pair of shoes

00:05:59.729 --> 00:06:05.030
that sport some Lightning McQueen stylings.
And Cars 3 director Brian Fee has confirmed

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:09.620
there are two Coco easter eggs in his movie,
one of which appears at the Rust-eze Racing

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.990
Center when a homesick car thinks of home
and a picture of the town from Coco appears

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:18.740
on one of the TV screens, and there's a second
nod to Coco in the background of another scene

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.669
when a car is on stage singing.

00:06:20.669 --> 00:06:25.730
There's a fabulous homage to Doc Hudson, aka
the Fabulous Hudson Hornet, when Lightning

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:29.620
changes his number and colours to Doc’s
and reveals he’s now the Fabulous Lightning

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.620
McQueen.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:35.080
So, which was your favourite easter egg in
Cars 3 and were there any you spotted that

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.830
I missed?
